# clang-tidy overrides for the Catch2 suite. Everything not listed below is
# inherited from the repository root configuration.
---
InheritParentConfig: true

Checks: >
  -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access,
  -cppcoreguidelines-special-member-functions,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.core.EnumCastOutOfRange

# Why these three, and only these three:
#
#   bugprone-unchecked-optional-access
#     Fires 25 times, all on values a REQUIRE has just asserted. The analysis
#     does not model Catch2's assertion macros, so it cannot see that the
#     optional is engaged. In engine code an unchecked access is undefined
#     behaviour; in a test it is a failing test, which is the point.
#
#   cppcoreguidelines-special-member-functions
#     Fixtures and RAII helpers under support/ are single-use scaffolding, not
#     value types with copy and move semantics worth spelling out. The rule
#     stays in force for everything the engine ships.
#   clang-analyzer-optin.core.EnumCastOutOfRange
#     False positive inside Catch2, which ORs two enumerators into a flags type.
#     Analyzer diagnostics ignore HeaderFilterRegex, so a vendored header cannot
#     be excluded any other way in this version. Still active for engine code.
